    overflow-x: auto;
  }

  .equation .frac {
    display: inline-flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    vertical-align: middle;
    margin: 0 0.2rem;
  }

  .equation .frac .num {
    border-bottom: 1.5px solid #333;
    padding: 0 0.3rem 0.1rem;
  }

  .equation .frac .den {
    padding: 0.1rem 0.3rem 0;
  }

  .equation sup { font-size: 0.7em; vertical-align: super; }
  .equation sub { font-size: 0.7em; vertical-align: sub; }

  .formula-block {
    background: #f4f9ff;
    border-left: 3px solid #6ab0f3;
    padding: 0.8rem 1.2rem;
    margin: 1rem 0;
    border-radius: 0 0.4rem 0.4rem 0;
    font-family: "Times New Roman", serif;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .columns {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .columns > div:first-child {
      border-right: none;
      border-bottom: 1px solid #e8f0f8;
    }
    header h1 { font-size: 1.5rem; }
    header p { font-size: 1rem; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<header>
  <h1>Why Is the Sky Blue?</h1>
  <p>天空为什么是蓝色的？</p>
</header>

<div class="container">

  <!-- Section 1: Toddler -->
  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <span class="icon">🧒</span>
      <h2>For a 3-Year-Old / 给三岁小朋友</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="columns">
      <div>
        <span class="lang-label">English</span>
        <div class="content">
          <p>When sunlight comes into our world, it's actually made of lots of tiny colors all mixed together — like a rainbow! The air around us is full of really, really tiny little specks (way too small to see). When the sunlight hits those tiny specks, the blue color bounces around the most, filling up the whole sky. That's why when you look up, you see all that pretty blue! It's like the sunshine is sprinkling blue glitter all over the sky for you. 🌈</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <span class="lang-label">中文</span>
        <div class="content">
          <p>当阳光来到我们的世界时，它其实是由好多好多小颜色混在一起组成的——就像彩虹一样！我们周围的空气里有很多很多特别特别小的微粒（小到完全看不见）。当阳光碰到这些微粒时，蓝色弹得最厉害，洒满了整个天空。所以当你抬起头，就能看到那片漂亮的蓝色啦！就像太阳把蓝色的亮片撒满了天空送给你一样。🌈</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Section 2: Teenager -->
  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <span class="icon">🎒</span>
      <h2>For a High School Teenager / 给高中生</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="columns">
      <div>
        <span class="lang-label">English</span>
        <div class="content">
          <p>Sunlight looks white, but it's actually a mix of all visible wavelengths (colors). When this light enters Earth's atmosphere, it interacts with gas molecules (mostly nitrogen and oxygen) through a process called <strong>Rayleigh scattering</strong>.</p>
          <p>The key physics: the intensity of scattered light is proportional to 1/λ⁴ (inverse fourth power of wavelength). Blue light has a shorter wavelength (~450 nm) compared to red light (~700 nm), so blue light is scattered roughly <strong>(700/450)⁴ ≈ 4.3 times more</strong> than red light. This is why the sky appears blue — blue light is scattered in all directions throughout the atmosphere.</p>
          <p>So why aren't eyes seeing violet, which has an even shorter wavelength (~400 nm)? Two reasons:</p>
          <ol>
            <li>The Sun emits less violet light than blue light.</li>
            <li>Human eyes are more sensitive to blue than violet.</li>
          </ol>
          <p>At sunset, sunlight travels through a much thicker path of atmosphere, scattering away most of the blue, leaving the reds and oranges to reach your eyes — hence sunsets.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <span class="lang-label">中文</span>
        <div class="content">
          <p>阳光看起来是白色的，但实际上它是所有可见波长（颜色）的混合。当这些光进入地球大气层时，会与气体分子（主要是氮气和氧气）发生一种叫做<strong>瑞利散射</strong>的相互作用。</p>
          <p>关键物理原理：散射光的强度与 1/λ⁴ 成正比（波长的四次方倒数）。蓝光的波长（约 450 nm）比红光（约 700 nm）短，因此蓝光被散射的程度大约是红光的 <strong>(700/450)⁴ ≈ 4.3 倍</strong>。这就是天空呈现蓝色的原因——蓝光在大气中向各个方向散射。</p>
          <p>那为什么我们看到的不是波长更短的紫色（约 400 nm）呢？两个原因：</p>
          <ol>
            <li>太阳发出的紫光比蓝光少。</li>
            <li>人眼对蓝色比对紫色更敏感。</li>
          </ol>
          <p>日落时，阳光穿过更厚的大气路径，大部分蓝光被散射掉了，剩下的红色和橙色到达你的眼睛——这就是日落的成因。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Section 3: PhD -->
  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <span class="icon">🎓</span>
      <h2>For a Physics PhD / 给物理学博士</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="columns">
      <div>
        <span class="lang-label">English</span>
        <div class="content">
          <p>The color of the sky arises from <strong>Rayleigh scattering</strong> of solar radiation by molecules in the atmosphere under the regime where the scattering particles are much smaller than the wavelength of incident light (<em>a</em> ≪ <em>λ</em>).</p>
          <p>The scattering cross-section for a single small particle with refractive index <em>n</em> relative to the medium is given by:</p>
          <div class="equation">
            σ = <span class="frac"><span class="num">8π³(n²−1)²</span><span class="den">3N²λ⁴</span></span>
          </div>
          <p>where <em>N</em> is the number density of molecules. The <em>λ</em><sup>−4</sup> dependence is the crucial spectral feature. For a clear, dry atmosphere, the single-scattering albedo and phase function (Rayleigh phase function, <em>P</em>(θ) = <span class="frac"><span class="num">3</span><span class="den">8π</span></span>(1+cos²θ)) determine the angular distribution of scattered light.</p>
          <p>The optical depth of a standard atmosphere is approximately τ<sub>λ</sub> ≈ 0.008 (λ/500 nm)<sup>−4</sup> · sec(<em>z</em>), where <em>z</em> is the zenith angle. For typical solar zenith angles, the atmosphere is optically thin (τ ≪ 1) in the visible, so single-scattering approximations hold.</p>
          <p>However, the full problem involves:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Mie scattering</strong> from aerosols (less wavelength-dependent, contributes to the whitening of the sky near the horizon and the "white" appearance of overcast skies)</li>
            <li><strong>Multiple scattering</strong> effects, which become non-negligible at large zenith angles and shift the perceived color</li>
            <li><strong>Atmospheric absorption</strong> (O₂ B-band at 687 nm, O₃ Chappuis band, and H₂O)</li>
            <li><strong>Ozone's red edge</strong>: the absorption spectrum of O₃ creates a slight shift in the sky color, particularly visible at twilight</li>
            <li><strong>Perceptual factors</strong>: the S-cone response and the contrast with the green of the lower sky influence the perceived hue. The sky is technically more azure (blue-green) than pure blue.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>A full radiative transfer solution requires integrating the radiative transfer equation:</p>
          <div class="equation">
            μ <span class="frac"><span class="num">dI</span><span class="den">dτ</span></span> = I − <span style="font-size:1.3em;vertical-align:-0.2em">∫</span><sub style="font-size:0.6em">4π</sub> P(ω′→ω) I(ω′) dω′ + S(ω)
          </div>
          <p>accounting for both Rayleigh and Mie scattering operators, absorption, and the solar source function, typically solved via discrete ordinate or Monte Carlo methods.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <span class="lang-label">中文</span>
        <div class="content">
          <p>天空的颜色源于大气分子对太阳辐射的<strong>瑞利散射</strong>，其中散射粒子的尺寸远小于入射光波长（<em>a</em> ≪ <em>λ</em>）。</p>
          <p>折射率为 <em>n</em>（相对于介质）的单个小粒子的散射截面为：</p>
          <div class="equation">
            σ = <span class="frac"><span class="num">8π³(n²−1)²</span><span class="den">3N²λ⁴</span></span>
          </div>
          <p>其中 <em>N</em> 是分子数密度。<em>λ</em><sup>−4</sup> 依赖关系是关键的光谱特征。对于晴朗干燥的大气，单散射反照率和相函数（瑞利相函数，<em>P</em>(θ) = <span class="frac"><span class="num">3</span><span class="den">8π</span></span>(1+cos²θ)）决定了散射光的角度分布。</p>
          <p>标准大气的光学厚度约为 τ<sub>λ</sub> ≈ 0.008 (λ/500 nm)<sup>−4</sup> · sec(<em>z</em>)，其中 <em>z</em> 为天顶角。对于典型的天顶角，大气在可见光范围内是光学薄的（τ ≪ 1），因此单散射近似成立。</p>
          <p>然而，完整的问题涉及：</p>
          <ul>
            <li>气溶胶的<strong>米氏散射</strong>（波长依赖性较弱，导致地平线附近天空变白以及阴天的"白色"外观）</li>
            <li><strong>多次散射</strong>效应，在大天顶角时变得不可忽略，并会改变感知颜色</li>
            <li><strong>大气吸收</strong>（O₂ 的 687 nm B 带、O₃ 的查普依斯带、以及 H₂O）</li>
            <li><strong>臭氧的红边效应</strong>：O₃ 的吸收光谱导致天空颜色的微小偏移，在黄昏时尤为明显</li>
            <li><strong>感知因素</strong>：S 型视锥细胞的响应以及与下方天空绿色的对比影响感知色相。严格来说，天空更接近天蓝色（蓝绿色）而非纯蓝色。</li>
          </ul>
          <p>完整的辐射传输求解需要积分辐射传输方程：</p>
          <div class="equation">
            μ <span class="frac"><span class="num">dI</span><span class="den">dτ</span></span> = I − <span style="font-size:1.3em;vertical-align:-0.2em">∫</span><sub style="font-size:0.6em">4π</sub> P(ω′→ω) I(ω′) dω′ + S(ω)
          </div>
          <p>同时考虑瑞利和米氏散射算子、吸收以及太阳源函数，通常通过离散纵标法或蒙特卡洛方法求解。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

</div>

<footer style="text-align:center; padding:2rem; color:#7a9bb8; font-size:0.85rem;">
  Why Is the Sky Blue? · 天空为什么是蓝色的？ · Bilingual Presentation
</footer>

<script>
  // Smooth scroll for sections on load
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const sections = document.querySelectorAll('.section');
    // Add subtle fade-in animation
    sections.forEach((section, i) => {
      section.style.opacity = '0';
      section.style.transform = 'translateY(20px)';
      section.style.transition = 'opacity 0.6s ease, transform 0.6s ease';
      setTimeout(() => {
        section.style.opacity = '1';
        section.style.transform = 'translateY(0)';
      }, 150 * (i + 1));
    });
  });
</script>

</body>
</html>
